      "id": "trusted-ereceipts-for-b2b-payments-issuing-verifiable-receipts-to-a-european-business-wallet-after-eudi-based-sca-yB3QzY",
      "sector": "finance",
      "title": "Trusted eReceipts for B2B Payments: Issuing verifiable receipts to a European Business Wallet after EUDI-based SCA",
      "summary": "Verifiable eReceipts for SME business purchases: An SME buys online. An authorised employee approves the payment with Strong Customer Authentication from their personal EUDI Wallet, and the signed receipt lands in the company's European Business Wallet, ready to post against input VAT.\n\nThat split is the hard part. Payment rails authenticate people; tax and audit are about organisations. Here the payer is a natural person, while the receipt is bound to the company's wallet key.\n\nFor SMEs, this replaces the paper slip that gets rekeyed, lost, or written off along with the VAT it could have evidenced. The eReceipt carries itemised lines, per-rate VAT and settlement evidence, so input VAT reconciles automatically once the buyer shares receipts with the Member State tax service. ViDA does this for invoices; nothing does it for receipts, where most SME spending happens.\n\nLive on the iGrant.io Organisation Wallet Suite and requires any EUDI Wallet app like Data Wallet.\n\nPiggy Bank (Buyer Bank): piggybank-demo.igrant.io\nSeller /Merchant: webuildshop-corporate-demo.igrant.io\nSME Business Wallet: byggab-businesswallet.igrant.io\nTax portal (demo): taxservice-demo.igrant.io",
