      "userJourney": "Onboarding:\n1. Buyer admin registers Bygg AB at the shop. The Business Wallet presents the company's legal identity (EBWOID) and VAT-ID; the shop stores where receipts go.\n2. Buyer admin adds authorised employees, each holding a payment attestation from their bank, Piggy Bank.\n\nPurchase:\n3. Employee Johan signs in to the shop in Business mode. The shop rechecks the company identity and his payment attestation.\n4. He checks out and approves the payment in his own personal EUDI Wallet with Strong Customer Authentication, linked to that transaction. Settlement is SEPA Instant.\n5. On settlement, the shop builds the eReceipt and issues it as a signed credential straight to the Bygg AB Business Wallet. No QR code, no app switching.\n6. The wallet verifies signature, issuer trust, integrity rules and revocation on arrival. Johan authenticated as a person; the receipt belongs to the company.\n\nReuse and Tax Reconciliation:\n7. The expense service books it as an expense (ReceiptHero, mocked here).\n8. Buyer admin shares the period's receipts with the Member State tax service.\n9. The tax portal verifies each receipt and reconciles input VAT per rate, with no rekeying on either side.",
